IC_kwDOCX47u85MUs_y","user":{"login":"mgurg","id":34517378,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NTE3Mzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34517378?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg","html_url":"https://github.com/mgurg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-10-17T08:40:05Z","updated_at":"2022-10-17T08:40:05Z","body":"Hi,\r\nI don't know if my today problem is related, but I have a error in the same area. With SQLAlchemy \"1.4.x\" everything was fine, after a switch to SQLAlchemy = \"2.0.0b1\" I am receiving:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nweb_1  | Not an executable object: 'set search_path to \"public\"'\r\nweb_1  | Traceback (most recent call last):\r\nweb_1  |   File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.10/site-packages/sqlalchemy/engine/base.py\", line 1388, in execute\r\nweb_1  |     meth = statement._execute_on_connection\r\nweb_1  | AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute '_execute_on_connection'\r\nweb_1  | \r\nweb_1  | The above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\r\nweb_1  | \r\nweb_1  | Traceback (most recent call last):\r\nweb_1  |   File \"/src/./app/service/tenants.py\", line 55, in alembic_upgrade_head\r\nweb_1  |     command.upgrade(config, revision, sql=sql, tag=tag)\r\nweb_1  |   File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.10/site-packages/alembic/command.py\", line 322, in upgrade\r\nweb_1  |     script.run_env()\r\nweb_1  |   File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.10/site-packages/alembic/script/base.py\", line 569, in run_env\r\nweb_1  |     util.load_python_file(self.dir, \"env.py\")\r\nweb_1  |   File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.10/site-packages/alembic/util/pyfiles.py\", line 94, in load_python_file\r\nweb_1  |     module = load_module_py(module_id, path)\r\nweb_1  |   File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.10/site-packages/alembic/util/pyfiles.py\", line 110, in load_module_py\r\nweb_1  |     spec.loader.exec_module(module)  # type: ignore\r\nweb_1  |   File \"<frozen importlib._bootstrap_external>\", line 883, in exec_module\r\nweb_1  |   File \"<frozen importlib._bootstrap>\", line 241, in _call_with_frames_removed\r\nweb_1  |   File \"/src/migrations/env.py\", line 103, in <module>\r\nweb_1  |     run_migrations_online()\r\nweb_1  |   File \"/src/migrations/env.py\", line 84, in run_migrations_online\r\nweb_1  |     connection.execute('set search_path to \"%s\"' % current_tenant)\r\nweb_1  |   File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.10/site-packages/sqlalchemy/engine/base.py\", line 1390, in execute\r\nweb_1  |     raise exc.ObjectNotExecutableError(statement) from err\r\nweb_1  | sqlalchemy.exc.ObjectNotExecutableError: Not an executable object: 'set search_path to \"public\"'\r\n```\r\n\r\nCode ( [Github repo](https://github.com/mgurg/fastapi_docker/blob/main/migrations/env.py)):\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef run_migrations_online() -> None:\r\n    \"\"\"Run migrations in 'online' mode.\r\n\r\n    In this scenario we need to create an Engine\r\n    and associate a connection with the context.\r\n\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    connectable = engine_from_config(\r\n        config.get_section(config.config_ini_section),\r\n        prefix=\"sqlalchemy.\",\r\n        poolclass=pool.NullPool,\r\n    )\r\n    current_tenant = context.get_x_argument(as_dictionary=True).get(\"tenant\")\r\n    dry_run = context.get_x_argument(as_dictionary=True).get(\"dry_run\")\r\n\r\n    with connectable.connect() as connection:\r\n        connection.execute('set search_path to \"%s\"' % current_tenant)\r\n        connection.dialect.default_schema_name = current_tenant\r\n\r\n        context.configure(\r\n            connection=connection,\r\n            target_metadata=target_metadata,\r\n            version_table_schema=current_tenant,\r\n        )\r\n\r\n        with context.begin_transaction() as transaction:\r\n            context.run_migrations()\r\n```\r\n**Versions.**\r\n- OS: Pop_os 22.04\r\n- Python: 3.10.7\r\n- Alembic: 1.8.1\r\n- SQLAlchemy: 1.4.42/2.0.0b1\r\n- Database: Postgres 14\r\n- DBAPI: psycopg2","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/1280495602/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"mgurg","id":34517378,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NTE3Mzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34517378?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg","html_url":"https://github.com/mgurg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgurg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/1280813787","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/1096#issuecomment-1280813787","issue_url":"http